              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for canvassing, then the Marathi for to be elected."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: लोकशाही",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लोकशाही — lokśāhī — \"democracy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लोकशाहीत जनता सरकार निवडते. lokśāhīt jantā sarkār nivaḍte. In a democracy, the people choose the government."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लोक + शाही, people + rule; the opposite is हुकूमशाही, dictatorship."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लोकशाही (lokśāhī) is a Marathi compound built from लोक, \"people\", from Sanskrit loka (Monier-Williams), and शाही, \"rule\", a loan from Persian shāhī, \"kingship\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
